  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/32ecd1d9-ea4e-42e6-ab78-8ade9bf117ff-image.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 183px;\" /></p><p>Recall the formula of the first law of thermodynamics in terms of change in internal energy and work done by the system,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>W</mi></math>, given,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>6000</mn><mn>60</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>100</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>90</mn><mi>t</mi></math>,&nbsp;<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>90</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>.</p>",
